    "q-71161": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71161",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int (-3{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (-3{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =-3\\int {x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{{x}^{4+1}}{4+1})+C \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
