    "q-71163": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71163",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{2{y}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{2{y}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {y}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{{y}^{-5+1}}{-5+1})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{{y}^{-4}}{-4})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {y}^{-4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8{y}^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
